# Bringing Insights from Research into the Teaching of Intermediate Macroeconomics.

**Authors:** Sheffrin, Steven M.

## Abstract
Argues that incorporating research into teaching intermediate macroeconomics can present challenging material to students thereby increasing their critical and evaluative thinking. Recommends sacrificing advanced textbook topics, historical perspectives on theories and policies, and current debates in favor of theoretical insights and empirical findings. (MJP)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ533344

